From: pierre-augustin <pierre.augustin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 15:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] beckham: audio: Route audio Moto Mods through usb-headset paths

The CAF audio HAL maps AUDIO_DEVICE_OUT_ANLG_DOCK_HEADSET, the device the
mod service connects for audio mods (e.g. JBL SoundBoost), to
SND_DEVICE_OUT_USB_HEADSET. mixer_paths.xml has no "usb-headset" path, so
the stream fails to start ("unable to find path 'usb-headset'",
"pcm_prepare returned -1") and nothing plays on the mod.

Alias the usb-headset paths to the existing mod paths, which route
SLIMBUS_0_RX to the codec AIF2 and set "Mods Enable Output Devices".

Test: JBL SoundBoost attached, media playback selects "usb-headset" and
applies "deep-buffer-playback usb-headset" without errors.

---
--- a/audio/mixer_paths.xml
+++ b/audio/mixer_paths.xml
@@ -1473,4 +1473,22 @@
 		<path name="mod-headset-mic" />
 		<ctl name="Mods Set Capture Use Case" value="Voice-Rec" />
 	</path>
+
+	<!-- Audio Moto Mods: the CAF audio HAL maps AUDIO_DEVICE_OUT_ANLG_DOCK_HEADSET
+	     (the device connected for the mod) to SND_DEVICE_OUT_USB_HEADSET -->
+	<path name="usb-headset">
+		<path name="mod-speaker" />
+	</path>
+
+	<path name="deep-buffer-playback usb-headset">
+		<path name="deep-buffer-playback mod" />
+	</path>
+
+	<path name="low-latency-playback usb-headset">
+		<path name="low-latency-playback mod" />
+	</path>
+
+	<path name="compress-offload-playback usb-headset">
+		<path name="compress-offload-playback mod" />
+	</path>
 </mixer>
